  "reason": "The current model underpredicts the magnitude of the negative trajectory in the held-out failure, by roughly 0.065–0.09 across the reported samples (failure_v3_r1_experiment_1). A term x*tanh(x)**2 is odd in x, so it can adjust the response magnitude at larger |x| while preserving the model's reset polarity symmetry. The polarity comparison for v3_r1 is consistent with that symmetry at the noise scale on the tested schedules (outcome_1); this is evidence for the tested inputs, not a universal law.",
